obmc-ikvm: no client, no busy loop

Without a VNC client the server thread waited in rfbProcessEvents() only
for one frame time (-f 60: 16.6 ms) and the video thread answered each
round: about 60 wakeups a second of two threads for nothing, ~4% of the
AST2500's one core all the time. Wait 0.25 s then: a connecting client
ends the wait at once (select() on the listening socket).

diff --git a/ikvm_server.cpp b/ikvm_server.cpp
index 65c298f..56c22ee 100644
--- a/ikvm_server.cpp
+++ b/ikvm_server.cpp
@@ -87,9 +87,14 @@ void Server::resize()
     }
 }
 
+// With no client the loop only waits for one: at the frame rate (-f 60) it
+// woke 60 times a second for nothing, ~4% of the BMC's one core. A client
+// connecting ends the wait at once (it is a select() on the listening socket).
+#define IDLE_WAIT_US 250000
+
 void Server::run()
 {
-    rfbProcessEvents(server, processTime);
+    rfbProcessEvents(server, server->clientHead ? processTime : IDLE_WAIT_US);
 
     if (server->clientHead)
     {
